<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fukuoka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fukuoka is the largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyushu">Kyushu</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fukuoka-prefecture">Fukuoka Prefecture</a>, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakata">Hakata</a> Bay facing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>. The area was an early gateway for contacts with the continent, from the Yayoi-period state of Na to the medieval port of Hakata. The castle town of Fukuoka was founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuroda-nagamasa">Kuroda Nagamasa</a> in 1601 and merged with Hakata in 1889 to form the modern city.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fukuoka.jpg" alt="Fukuoka" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nryate · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fukuoka_Skyline_of_Seaside_Momochi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
